From bf99b284afc1de59bcebbb585af45f98759397bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bernhard=20Rosenkr=C3=A4nzer?= <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:52:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xfree86: default SingleDriver to true

XLibre 25.2 still autoconfigures modesetting/fbdev/vesa as fallbacks
after a successful amdgpu (or other DDX) probe, then lets more than one
driver add non-GPU screens. modesetting's old probe then opens the same
KMS device, drmSetMaster fails with EBUSY, and the server exits.

A given DRM node can only have one master. Secondary GPUs for offload
still work: xf86BusConfig() only stops additional primary screens;
platform GPU screens are added afterwards.

Closes: https://github.com/OpenMandrivaAssociation/distribution/issues/3532
---
 hw/xfree86/common/xf86Globals.c | 2 +-
 hw/xfree86/man/xorg.conf.man    | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Globals.c b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Globals.c
index 336e089..ee58ce1 100644
--- a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Globals.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Globals.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@ xf86InfoRec xf86Info = {
     .autoAddGPU = FALSE,
 #endif
     .autoBindGPU = TRUE,
-    .singleDriver = FALSE,
+    .singleDriver = TRUE,
 };
 
 const char *xf86ConfigFile = NULL;
diff --git a/hw/xfree86/man/xorg.conf.man b/hw/xfree86/man/xorg.conf.man
index 1d0d821..ca524dd 100644
--- a/hw/xfree86/man/xorg.conf.man
+++ b/hw/xfree86/man/xorg.conf.man
@@ -691,7 +691,7 @@ Allow clients with a different byte-order than the server. Disabled by default.
 .BI "Option \*qSingleDriver\*q  \*q" boolean \*q
 Only the first successfully probed driver is allowed to add screens to the current layout, others may
 add secondary GPU screens only (e.g., if non-primary GPUs are used for offloading).
-Disabled by default.
+Enabled by default.
 .SH "MODULE SECTION"
 The
 .B Module
